  "worked_solution": "The level surfaces of the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ \\frac{3z}{x+6y} & =c \\\\ 3z & =c(x+6y) \\\\ 3z & =cx+6cy \\\\ z & =\\frac{c}{3}x+2cy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get a family of planes:\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{c}{3}x+2cy,\\,c\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$",
